-

I don't remember if we discussed this:

Is it possible to insert Google Maps or iframes into articles in the Lojban 
Mediawiki (http://mw.lojban.org)?
I wanted to put a Google Map of world Lojbanists in an article:
https://maps.google.com/maps/ms?msid=210623699789786150712.0004b8e4decb3f8be5c33&msa=0&ll=28.613459,3.515625&spn=140.083619,324.492188&z=2
But I don't think the Mediawiki can do that right now. I believe it needs 
either a Widget capability, an iframe capability, or a Google Maps 
extension.

I think this looks like the right thing:
http://www.mediawikiwidgets.org/Google_Maps

Which means this extension would need to be installed: 
http://www.mediawiki.org/wiki/Extension:Widget


Does this sound like a good idea?
.i xu la'e ro di'u cu xaumlu

mu'o mi'e .vruxir.

